-- Q7661: Public Company Reporting [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 260-10-45-28 and ASC 718, stock compensation expense flows through net income, reducing the basic EPS numerator. Separately, the outstanding options create incremental shares under the treasury stock method for diluted EPS. These are two distinct effects: one on the numerator and one on the denominator.
Wrong (A): Although stock compensation is noncash, it is recognized in the income statement and reduces net income; it is not added back for EPS purposes.
Wrong (C): The options do affect diluted EPS through incremental shares in the denominator; recognizing the expense does not eliminate the dilutive share effect.
Wrong (D): Stock compensation expense reduces net income and therefore reduces EPS; it does not increase EPS or reduce shares outstanding.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 7661;

